            "began_copy": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Online, a saree was four photos and a paragraph. No weight, no drape, no way to know whether the silk was silk. I bought things that arrived nothing like the picture, and I stopped trusting the whole category.</p><p>So in 2016 I started IndyVogue out of my garage in Austin, with a handful of pieces from weavers I already knew back home. I photographed every one myself.</p>",
                "hidden_br_mobile": false,
                "hidden_on_mobile": false,
                "ffamily": "",
                "text_size": "2xl",
                "line_height": "",
                "font_weight": "normal",
